Subject: [PATCH] Add in-page mobile tabs to Dashboard to reduce scrolling

The Dashboard stacks 13+ sections vertically (quick actions, priority
board, metrics, business profile, checks, action center, appointment
snapshots, payroll runs, leaderboard, commission profile, booth rent),
all shown at once. On mobile that meant a long scroll through
everything just to check one thing.

Added a small tab bar (Overview / Actions / Appointments / Payroll)
that groups these sections, mobile-only, at max-width: 900px. Each
section got a data-mobile-group attribute and a conditional
is-active-mobile-tab class; the CSS hides non-active groups only
below that breakpoint. Desktop is completely unchanged -- every
section still renders exactly as before, all at once, regardless of
tab state.

Verified: production build succeeds with no errors, and a computed-
style check confirms mobile shows only the active group with the tab
bar visible, while desktop shows every group with the tab bar
hidden.
